{"_comment":"Example daemon.json. Copy to ~/.napcat-data/daemon.json (gitignored) and fill real values. Generated automatically by 'napcat daemon start'; editting by hand is fine but 'napcat daemon start' will rewrite it from NapCatConfig config.json — set values via 'napcat config set <key> <value>' to persist.","self_id":"","wake_command":"","wake_on_event":true,"ws_port":18800,"ws_url":"","http_port":18821,"api_url":"http://127.0.0.1:18800","token":"","group_trigger_word":"","private_trigger":"*","skills_fs_enabled":true,"skills_fs_mountpoint":"$HOME/.hermes/skills/napcat-cli","skills_fs_binary":"$HOME/.local/bin/skills-fs","skills_fs_config":"$HOME/.napcat-data/skills-fs.json","wake_enabled":true,"wake_preset":"hermes","wake_primary":"http","wake_session":"napcat-qq","wake_http_url":"","wake_http_session_id":"","wake_cli_command":"","wake_debounce_seconds":3,"wake_cooldown_seconds":30,"wake_new_message_idle_seconds":600,"_docker_crossmapping_note":"If NapCat runs in Docker, the host port may be CROSS-mapped vs the container OneBot11 port (e.g. host 18800 -> container 3000 HTTP, host 18801 -> container 3001 WS). In that case set api_url=http://127.0.0.1:18800 (HTTP) and ws_url=ws://127.0.0.1:18801 (WS). Keep token in sync with NapCat's onebot11_<selfid>.json network.{httpServers,websocketServers} token field."}